[05/10/26]	script.c
		"Dump current state" turns out to already exist in RasMol
		2.6b2: "write script <file>" (also "write rasmol <file>" or
		"save script <file>") already serialises the entire live
		session - loaded molecule, view (rotation/zoom/slab), per-
		atom colours and selection, every representation (cartoon/
		ribbons/backbone/dots/labels/monitors), H-bond/SS-bond
		display - to a replayable .rsc script. It just wasn't
		mentioned in this fork's README, so this was unknown.
		Found and fixed a real bug in it while verifying this against
		this fork's main feature: WriteScriptFile()'s DataFileFormat
		switch (used to generate the dumped script's "load" line) was
		missing FormatCIF entirely, predating the mmCIF reader this
		fork added - it fell through to the "default: pdb" case, so
		"write script" on any CIF-loaded molecule emitted
		"load pdb \"foo.cif\"" instead of "load cif \"foo.cif\"",
		silently misparsing the mmCIF text as fixed-column PDB on
		replay - the exact flattened/garbage-coordinate failure mode
		already fixed for the normal load path, reintroduced here.
		Confirmed concretely on pdb/1mbn.cif: replaying the old buggy
		"load pdb" line on this file produces 136 phantom chains and
		wrong bond counts (784 vs. the correct 1292) from the same
		1216 atoms. Added the missing FormatCIF case (and FormatNMRPDB,
		same gap, lower-stakes since it just loses the NMR-multi-model
		flag rather than misparsing). Verified fixed: dumped script
		now emits "load cif ...", replays cleanly, no errors. Full
		regression suite (1mbn, 7dns, 1bmf, 7ahl, 3cro) re-run byte-
		identical to pre-change output.

[05/10/26]	(repo cleanup, no source changes)
		Removed dead weight from the tree:
		 - cexio.c: never built (CEXIOLIB is permanently commented
		   out in rasmol.h, and the file isn't in Makefile's SRCS at
		   all), fully unwired dead code.
